From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:14:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! logging: write log lines on a logger thread

Apply the new log fixture path with Flush before starting rotation producers. A larger ring can remain below the wake threshold during the first rename, so waiting three milliseconds did not guarantee the file had been opened. The real rotation unit aborted before; an isolated paused-logger control fails without this barrier and passes with it.
---
 src/test/logging_tests.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/test/logging_tests.cpp b/src/test/logging_tests.cpp
index 1c33a03acc..1b5a84c610 100644
--- a/src/test/logging_tests.cpp
+++ b/src/test/logging_tests.cpp
@@ -874,6 +874,10 @@ BOOST_FIXTURE_TEST_CASE(logging_async_flush, LogSetup) {
 }
 
 BOOST_FIXTURE_TEST_CASE(logging_async_reopen_under_load, LogSetup) {
+    // Apply the fixture path before rename. A lightly filled larger ring may
+    // otherwise remain below its wake threshold during the first rotation.
+    LogInstance().Flush();
+
     // The log file is rotated (renamed, then reopened) while a thread logs:
     // every line is in exactly one of the files, in order, unless it was
     // dropped because the thread outran the logger (counted).
